@startmindmap
title = The ReAct loop and it's mapping to chat roles
*[#orange] = ReAct

**[#yellow]:== Concepts
and Components;

***:=== Prompt
Our ask of the LLM. This includes the list of 
allowable actions that it can take;
***:=== Actions
Action is a **verb** that the LLM needs 
to **do** in the process of building out 
the response to the prompt.

An action is simply the LLM Tool we have 
seen before: the //function call//;

***:=== Observations
The **outcome of an action** is called
the observation. This was named to imply 
that the LLM is //doing stuff// and then 
//observing// what happens.

In tool terms, this is the return value of 
the function call;

***:=== Answer
Once the LLM has taken all the actions it 
needs to and made the consequent 
observations it finally decides that it has 
enough information to provide a final answer;

